---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Uses" description="Tools and setup notes for Anusha Dharmasena.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 pb-10 pt-16 md:pb-14 md:pt-24">
    <div class="surface-card-strong rounded-[2rem] p-8 md:p-10">
      <p class="section-label">Uses</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-5xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.06em] text-white md:text-7xl md:leading-[0.96]">The tools I actually reach for, not an aspirational gear list.</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300 md:text-xl">
        This page exists so I can point at the setup and defaults that genuinely help me ship. It is intentionally short.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-8 md:py-10">
    <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="surface-card rounded-[2rem] p-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] text-white">Core setup</h2>
        <ul class="mt-5 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-300">
          <li>macOS on Apple silicon.</li>
          <li>VS Code and Cursor, depending on the job.</li>
          <li>TypeScript and JavaScript first, Python when it is the simplest answer.</li>
          <li>Git and GitHub for anything I want to keep, revisit, or explain properly.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="surface-card rounded-[2rem] p-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] text-white">Working preferences</h2>
        <ul class="mt-5 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-300">
          <li>Fast local feedback over elaborate ceremony.</li>
          <li>Readable code before clever code.</li>
          <li>Tools that reduce friction without trying to become the whole job.</li>
          <li>Defaults that are easy to live with six months later.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
